BT /F1 9 Tf 54 760 Td 12 TL (Bond maths: the fixed-coupon street convention) Tj T* () Tj T* (FinTekkers knowledge library. Written in our own words for golden cases and) Tj T* (reviews; the primary sources are listed at the end. Notation: C is the annual) Tj T* (coupon per 100 face, f the coupons per year, y the annual yield quoted at) Tj T* (frequency f, R the redemption amount per 100 \(normally 100\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (1 Scope {#scope}) Tj T* () Tj T* (This document fixes how FinTekkers prices a plain fixed-coupon bond between) Tj T* (coupon dates: the period fraction, accrued interest, dirty and clean price,) Tj T* (yield, Macaulay and modified duration, convexity and DV01. It is the) Tj T* (convention US Treasuries and US corporates are quoted on, and the one) Tj T* (spreadsheet functions such as PRICE, YIELD and MDURATION implement. Floating,) Tj T* (zero-coupon and callable bonds are out of scope.) Tj T* () Tj T* (2 Coupon schedule and the period fraction {#coupon-schedule}) Tj T* () Tj T* (Coupon dates step back from maturity in whole periods of 12/f months, on the) Tj T* (maturity day of the month \(end-of-month bonds stay on month ends\). For a) Tj T* (settlement date S:) Tj T* () Tj T* (- PCD is the last coupon date on or before S, NCD the first one after S.) Tj T* (- E is the number of days in the period PCD to NCD \(actual days for) Tj T* (  ACT/ACT ICMA, see the day-count document\).) Tj T* (- A is the accrued days, PCD to S, under the bond's day count.) Tj T* (- DSC is the days from S to NCD, so DSC = E - A.) Tj T* (- w = DSC / E is the period fraction: the part of the current period still) Tj T* (  to run, with 0 < w <= 1.) Tj T* (- n is the number of coupons still to be paid, NCD included.) Tj T* () Tj T* (On a coupon date w = 1 and nothing has accrued. One day before a coupon date) Tj T* (w is close to 0.) Tj T* () Tj T* (3 Accrued interest {#accrued}) Tj T* () Tj T* (Accrued interest per 100 face is the coupon earned since PCD:) Tj T* () Tj T* (    AI = \(C / f\) * A / E) Tj T* () Tj T* (For a bond on 30/360 US, A is the 30/360 day count from PCD to S and E is) Tj T* (360 / f, so a full period is always 180 days for a semiannual bond. The) Tj T* (buyer pays the clean price plus AI. Ex-dividend periods are not modelled.) Tj T* () Tj T* (4 The fractional first period {#first-period-stub}) Tj T* () Tj T* (Between coupon dates the first cash flow is only w periods away, not a full) Tj T* (period. Every flow is therefore discounted over k + w periods, where k counts) Tj T* (whole periods from NCD \(k = 0 for NCD itself\). Treating the first period as a) Tj T* (whole one \(discounting over k + 1\) mis-states every time to cash flow by) Tj T* (1 - w periods. That error moves yield, duration and convexity together, and it) Tj T* (vanishes only when settlement falls on a coupon date \(w = 1\), which is why a) Tj T* (test that settles on a coupon date cannot catch it.) Tj T* () Tj T* (An irregular first coupon from issue \(short or long first coupon\) changes the) Tj T* (amount of the first coupon and how AI is counted inside that period. The) Tj T* (fraction w is still measured inside the notional regular period that contains) Tj T* (S.) Tj T* ET
