BT /F1 9 Tf 54 760 Td 12 TL () Tj T* (5 Dirty and clean price {#price}) Tj T* () Tj T* (The dirty \(full\) price per 100 at yield y is the present value of the) Tj T* (remaining flows, discounted from S:) Tj T* () Tj T* (    P_dirty = sum over k = 0 .. n-1 of \(C/f\) / \(1 + y/f\)^\(k + w\)) Tj T* (              + R / \(1 + y/f\)^\(n - 1 + w\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (    P_clean = P_dirty - AI) Tj T* () Tj T* (Quotes are clean; the calculation is done on dirty. When only one coupon is) Tj T* (left \(n = 1\), US street practice and the spreadsheet functions use simple) Tj T* (interest instead: P_dirty = \(R + C/f\) / \(1 + w * y / f\). A golden case in the) Tj T* (final period must say which of the two forms it uses.) Tj T* () Tj T* (6 Yield to maturity {#yield}) Tj T* () Tj T* (The yield is the y that makes P_dirty in section 5 equal to the quoted clean) Tj T* (price plus AI. It is quoted annualised at the coupon frequency \(a) Tj T* (bond-equivalent yield for a semiannual bond\). There is no closed form: solve) Tj T* (numerically. A Newton-Raphson solve on y uses dP/dy from section 8, starts) Tj T* (from the current yield C / P_clean, stops when the price error is below a) Tj T* (stated tolerance \(1e-10 per 100 is ample\), and reports failure after a capped) Tj T* (number of iterations instead of returning the last iterate.) Tj T* () Tj T* (7 Macaulay duration {#macaulay-duration}) Tj T* () Tj T* (Macaulay duration is the present-value-weighted average time to the cash) Tj T* (flows, in years. With t_k = k + w periods and PV_k the discounted value of) Tj T* (flow k at the solved yield:) Tj T* () Tj T* (    D_mac = \(1 / f\) * \(sum of t_k * PV_k\) / P_dirty) Tj T* () Tj T* (The weights use the dirty price, the same one the yield was solved on.) Tj T* () Tj T* (8 Modified duration {#modified-duration}) Tj T* () Tj T* (Modified duration is the relative price change for a small change in yield:) Tj T* () Tj T* (    D_mod = -\(1 / P_dirty\) * dP_dirty/dy = D_mac / \(1 + y/f\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (It inherits the fractional first period from D_mac. A duration built from) Tj T* (whole periods overstates D_mac by \(1 - w\) / f years before the division, and a) Tj T* (yield solved on the clean price instead of the dirty price shifts it again.) Tj T* () Tj T* (9 Convexity and DV01 {#convexity}) Tj T* () Tj T* (Convexity is the second derivative of the dirty price, scaled by price, in) Tj T* (years squared:) Tj T* () Tj T* (    Convexity = \(1 / P_dirty\) * \(1 / f^2\)) Tj T* (                * sum of t_k * \(t_k + 1\) * CF_k / \(1 + y/f\)^\(t_k + 2\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (where CF_k is the flow paid at t_k. DV01 is the change in dirty price for a) Tj T* (one basis point fall in yield, per 100 face: DV01 = D_mod * P_dirty * 0.0001.) Tj T* (A central finite difference of P_dirty with a 1bp bump each way is a good) Tj T* (independent check of both.) Tj T* ET
